{%- comment -%}
  fye-swatch-block — a metal or gemstone as a full-bleed colour field.

  Added 05/09/2026. Ed, with a screenshot of the metal step: "the swatches
  don't really match the look and feel of the site."

  WHY A NEW SNIPPET RATHER THAN CHANGING THE OLD ONE. fye-metal-swatch is the
  product page's swatch, and Ed asked for those specifically ("can you use the
  same swatches used in the product pages"). Editing it to fix the finder would
  change every product page as a side effect. So the product swatch is left
  exactly as it is and the finder gets its own treatment.

  WHAT WAS WRONG. The product swatch is a small object sat next to text: a
  25x25 field with its own hairline inside a 30x30 box. Correct at 20px beside
  a variant name. Scaled to fill a 200px tile it became three nested rectangles
  — the tile's border, the swatch's margin, the swatch's own stroke — which
  reads as a framed picture of a colour rather than a material.

  WHAT THIS IS. One colour field, edge to edge, no stroke and no margin: the
  tile's own hairline is the only frame, so a metal tile is built exactly like
  the ring photograph tiles beside it. The sheen is a single soft diagonal —
  enough to say polished metal, not a highlight drawn on top.

  USAGE
    {%- render 'fye-swatch-block', kind: 'metal', name: 'Rose Gold' -%}
    {%- render 'fye-swatch-block', kind: 'gem',   name: 'Sapphire'  -%}

  Self-contained: each render carries its own gradient with a unique id, so
  there is no page-level defs block to remember and no id collision when the
  same metal appears on two steps.

  NOTE ON THE COLOUR TABLE. This was first written with explanatory comments
  inside the case block, which threw "Case tag must be followed by exactly one
  'when'" and blanked the section. Liquid allows ONLY when/else between case
  and endcase. Hence the notes live here:

    · metals — light and dark stop lifted off the product swatch, so a finder
      swatch and a product swatch read as the same metal.
    · stones — the mega-menu's own hex as the dark stop, a shade lighter for
      the light stop.
    · blue topaz IS topaz, pink tourmaline IS tourmaline: the finder's names
      carry a qualifier the stone itself does not, so both map to one colour.
    · an unknown name falls through to the ivory ground, so a typo in the theme
      editor shows as a blank stone rather than a broken tile.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign key = name | strip | downcase | replace: ' ', '-'
  if kind == 'gem' and key == 'blue-topaz'
    assign key = 'topaz'
  endif
  if kind == 'gem' and key == 'pink-tourmaline'
    assign key = 'tourmaline'
  endif

  case key
    when 'platinum'
      assign a = '#E7E9EA'
      assign b = '#C4C9CB'
    when 'yellow-gold'
      assign a = '#EDD584'
      assign b = '#C7A340'
    when 'white-gold'
      assign a = '#F4F5F5'
      assign b = '#D8DBDB'
    when 'rose-gold'
      assign a = '#F2CDB8'
      assign b = '#D69E82'
    when 'palladium'
      assign a = '#E5E7E8'
      assign b = '#BFC4C6'
    when 'ruby'
      assign a = '#B32438'
      assign b = '#8A1526'
    when 'sapphire'
      assign a = '#244C86'
      assign b = '#16305A'
    when 'emerald'
      assign a = '#228557'
      assign b = '#155839'
    when 'tanzanite'
      assign a = '#6C5FBE'
      assign b = '#4C4192'
    when 'aquamarine'
      assign a = '#A6D7E7'
      assign b = '#79B6CD'
    when 'morganite'
      assign a = '#F1C2BB'
      assign b = '#DC9E95'
    when 'peridot'
      assign a = '#AFCC4E'
      assign b = '#87A52E'
    when 'amethyst'
      assign a = '#9E60BC'
      assign b = '#753F93'
    when 'garnet'
      assign a = '#93222E'
      assign b = '#69141D'
    when 'citrine'
      assign a = '#EFB13A'
      assign b = '#CE8C1C'
    when 'topaz'
      assign a = '#55A5DA'
      assign b = '#2E7EB6'
    when 'opal'
      assign a = '#F5F1E9'
      assign b = '#E2DACB'
    when 'tourmaline'
      assign a = '#E27AAD'
      assign b = '#C74E88'
    when 'diamond'
      assign a = '#FBFCFC'
      assign b = '#E4E9EA'
    when 'fire-opal'
      assign a = '#E8873A'
      assign b = '#C4600F'
    when 'black-diamond'
      assign a = '#3A3D40'
      assign b = '#1E2022'
    else
      assign a = '#F5F1E9'
      assign b = '#E2DACB'
  endcase

  assign uid = 'sw-' | append: kind | append: '-' | append: key
-%}
<svg class="fic fic--block fic--block-{{ key }} {{ class }}" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="{{ name | escape }}" focusable="false">
  <defs>
    <linearGradient id="{{ uid }}" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
      <stop offset="0" stop-color="{{ a }}"></stop>
      <stop offset="1" stop-color="{{ b }}"></stop>
    </linearGradient>
    <linearGradient id="{{ uid }}-s" x1="0" y1="1" x2="1" y2="0">
      <stop offset="0.28" stop-color="#FFFFFF" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
      <stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#FFFFFF" stop-opacity="0.22"></stop>
      <stop offset="0.72" stop-color="#FFFFFF" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
    </linearGradient>
  </defs>
  <rect width="100" height="100" fill="url(#{{ uid }})"></rect>
  <rect width="100" height="100" fill="url(#{{ uid }}-s)"></rect>
</svg>
